																		Author Notes
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1404533&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607353347" alt="Zyn" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1404533)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;" >Zyn</a></span> <span class="odate time_1437262339 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">18 Jul 2015 23:32</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2340833">
									

<p>Many thanks to these awesome people (if I forgot anyone, please remind me!):</p>
<ul>
<li>EldrichCyanide, Dr_Leonard, Dexanote and for looking over it in chat</li>
<li>Riemann and Dmatix for being tough on the plot development, especially interview</li>
<li>Eskobar and Photosynthetic for wording</li>
<li>FiestaSheep and Davsto who gave some animal ideas</li>
<li>Wogglebug for overview and phrasing</li>
<li>MisterFlames for help with feel and cat breed suggestion</li>
<li>Vivax for help with SCIENCE and teaching me bauplan and for the patience to properly convey the feels.</li>
<li>Drewbear for helping with emotion evocation</li>
<li>Cimmerian for edits and trimming (oh man lots of trimming)</li>
<li>MacLeod and Eta Carinae for feedback in the forums!</li>
<li>Silber for the name. Silber is good at naming.</li>
</ul>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Author&nbsp;ramblings</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Marp</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Also known as “man, Zyn misses that one neighborhood cat that used to visit her and her friend in the evenings”. Plants are nice and about all I have time for, but cuddling and doting on a plant feels silly and a little sad.</p>
<p>This sort of grew out of a lot of things. One was the thought, “no one will look twice if you see a cat you don’t know walking around and pet it or cuddle it, but no one does that to a person they don’t know”. And yet people find Tesla strange for loving a pigeon.</p>
<p>There was also an <a href="http://www.dailymail.co.uk/sciencetech/article-1027637/The-tame-baby-sharks-DONT-bite-hand-feeds-them.html">article about aquarium sharks</a> I read awhile back that I’d wanted to write something alluding to at one point.</p>
<p>And also there was that video of a swallow crying when its mate died. Animal emotion is something I wonder a lot about. I wonder how those experiences compare to those of humans. Is simplicity preferable? How does depth factor in?</p>
<p>Edit because can't emphasize enough: the interview went through a <em>ton</em> of revisions, with a bunch of reviewers. Mood was changed, it went from blunt to emo teenager to too obfuscated etc. etc. Many thanks for the patience and the advice, you all.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Spoiler&nbsp;alert</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Alert&nbsp;alert.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>It’s a vicious cycle. The less “happy” this thing is, the more animal-like it regresses into acting, because that’s the only way it knows how to get more of that unconditional human affection it has always craved. Being an animal for so long takes its toll.</p>
<p>This poor thing has no control over any of its abilities. It just knows what it wants… or at least it thinks it does.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>The picture is from the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brownbanded_bamboo_shark">Brown-banded bamboo shark Wikipedia article</a>, and licensed under <a href="http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Main_Page">Wikimedia Commons</a>.</p>

							</div>

								
