<p>The thing being unable to control its ability(ies) is a focal point, yeah.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Spoilers&nbsp;or&nbsp;ramblings?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">bit&nbsp;of&nbsp;both,&nbsp;I&nbsp;guess.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The thing is only a butterfly bamboo shark that can write kanji <em>at the moment</em> because that's a form ideally matched to its current caretaker (Researcher Kiryu is half Chinese, half Japanese, likes butterflies and sharks, and studies biological anomalies).</p>
<p>The Foundation's seen how many forms this thing is capable of, and now that it can communicate, it's worth keeping the shark in that form instead of testing with various personnel until they get another form that can communicate.</p>
<p>My headcanon is that the thing doesn't actually remember anything. But it doesn't know that. Its memories are unstable, and are warped as necessary, just as its body is, to trigger sympathy.</p>
</div>
